      "the_reaction": "⚗️ The reaction",
      "the_real_biology_behind_it": "🔬 The real biology behind it",
      "the_right_principle_leave_the_animal_i": "The right principle: leave the animal in a state where it doesn't know you were there. You can take photos + memories. Take nothing physical.",
      "the_shape_of_the_visual_cortex": "The shape of the visual cortex",
      "the_shift_from_monster_to_mind_is_one_": "The shift from monster to mind is one of the largest cultural reframings in recent biology. It happened fast — in roughly 50 years — driven by a small number of researchers + filmmakers + writers + activists. The cephalopods themselves didn't change. Our way of seeing them did.",
      "the_simulator_is_a_tool_not_a_curricul": "The simulator is a tool, not a curriculum. Pair it with reading, discussion, writing, and reflection. The most effective uses I've seen:\n\n(1) HOOK — open with the simulator. Project on big screen. Let students see camouflage in action before any vocabulary. Then introduce vocabulary as their CURIOSITY demands it.\n\n(2) EVIDENCE — use the simulator to GENERATE DATA students can analyze. Multi-trial runs + data tables + class comparisons.\n\n(3) DISCUSSION — use the simulator as a SHARED REFERENCE for class discussions. \"Remember when the moray eel attacked? What did the octopus do? Why might that work?\"\n\n(4) ASSESSMENT — use the simulator as an authentic performance task. Students can demonstrate understanding by what they DO in the simulator, not just what they write.\n\n(5) REFLECTION — close with the simulator. After 2 weeks of study, ask students to predict what would happen in different scenarios. Test their predictions.",
      "the_siphon_is_the_muscular_tube_that_w": "The siphon is the muscular tube that water exits during jet propulsion. It's STEERABLE — the octopus can point it forward, backward, up, down. Jet through siphon = thrust in opposite direction. Squid use this for explosive escape (up to 25 m/s in Humboldt squid). Octopuses use it gently for steering + as a secondary swim mode (primary mode is arm-crawling).",
      "the_smallest_cephalopod_idiosepius_pyg": "The smallest cephalopod (Idiosepius pygmaeus, the pygmy squid) is only 1.5 cm long. The largest (colossal squid) reaches 14 m and 750 kg.",
      "the_soul_of_an_octopus_a_surprising_ex": "The Soul of an Octopus: A Surprising Exploration into the Wonder of Consciousness",
      "the_soul_of_an_octopus_young_reader_s_": "The Soul of an Octopus (Young Reader's Edition)",
      "the_species_has_survived_500_million_y": "The species has survived 500 million years of evolution essentially unchanged. It may not survive the past 30 years of shell collecting.",
      "the_squid_emerges_to_hunt_bacterial_bi": "The squid emerges to hunt. Bacterial bioluminescence pours from the ventral light organ at ~moonlight brightness — matching downwelling moonlight to erase its silhouette from predators below.",
      "the_squid_giant_axon_papers": "The squid giant axon papers",
      "the_squid_returns_to_its_sandy_hideout": "The squid returns to its sandy hideout as light begins to creep across the eastern sky. The cycle prepares to reset at dawn.",
