      "real_bats_use_frequencies_of_20_200_kh": "🦇 Real bats use frequencies of 20-200 kHz (ultrasonic). Humans echolocate best with tongue clicks at 2-4 kHz. The key cue is the time delay between click and echo — at 343 m/s, a wall 1.7m away returns an echo in 10ms.",
